    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "In this paper, we use curvature method to predict subsurface fracture density and orientation in Liaohe Oil field Northeastern China. The hypothesis is that fractures in fold are mathematically related to the curvature defined by the deflection of a thin elastic plate.\r\n\r\nThe Bian Tai Anticline of Liaohe Oil Field in Northeastern China is a typical fractured reservoir. The anticline was formed in response to a North- south directed compression and twisting movement during bending. Joint clusters appear to be the major fracture system in the reservoir. We present the calculated distribution of fracture density at various depths in the reservoir.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
